#: tips.cc:3
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can synchronize your calendar data with the data on a Palm "
"Pilot\n"
"by using <a href=\"http://www.slac.com/pilone/kpilot_home\">KPilot</a>?\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:8
msgid ""
"<p>...that it is possible to show the current time in the calendar? Enable "
"the\n"
"Marcus Bains line in the dialog which appears after selecting <b>Settings</"
"b>, \n"
"<b>KOrganizer settings...</b> from the menu bar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:14
msgid ""
"<p>...that KOrganizer supports Microsoft Exchange? Just enable the plugin\n"
"<b>Microsoft Exchange 2000 plugin for KOrganizer</b> in the dialog\n"
"<b>Configure Plugins...</b> from the <b>Settings</b> menu.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:20
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can select whether the week starts on Monday or on Sunday in "
"the KDE\n"
"Control Center? KOrganizer uses this setting. Look at Personalization-"
">Country &\n"
"Languages, on the Time & Dates tab.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:26
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can edit todo's quickly by right clicking on the property "
"you\n"
"wish to change; like the priority, the category or the date?\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:31
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can view and edit a calendar from the shell with\n"
"konsolekalendar? Run <b>konsolekalendar --help</b> for the available "
"options.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:36
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can import birthdays from your address book? There is a "
"resource\n"
"available which connects the birthdays to your calendar; it is even possible "
"to\n"
"set a reminder for each event.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:42
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can store your calendar on an FTP server? Use the standard "
"file\n"
"dialog to save the calendar to a URL like <b>ftp://username@ftpserver/"
"filename</b>.\n"
"You can make your calendar active and load and save it as if it were local.\n"
"Just make sure that no two KOrganizer applications are working on the same "
"file, at\n"
"the same time.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:50
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can create hierarchical To-Dos by clicking with the right "
"mouse\n"
"button on an existing To-Do and selecting <b>New Sub-To-Do</b> from the "
"context menu?\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:55
msgid ""
"<p>...that a color can be assigned to each category? Events with a certain\n"
"category will be shown in that color. You can assign these in the section\n"
"<b>Colors</b> within the dialog which appears after selecting <b>Settings</"
"b>, \n"
"<b>KOrganizer settings...</b> from the menu bar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:62
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can view and edit a calendar with Konqueror? Just click on "
"the\n"
"calendar file to make Konqueror open it.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:67
msgid ""
"<p>...that it is possible to add an attachment to an event? To do so, add a "
"link\n"
"to the <b>Attachments</b> tab within the <b>Edit Event</b> dialog.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:72
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can export your calendar to HTML? Check the plugin\n"
"<b>Web export plugin for KOrganizer</b> in the dialog <b>Configure\n"
"Plugins...</b> from the <b>Settings</b> menu. Now you can export your "
"calendar\n"
"with <b>File</b>, <b>Export</b>, <b>Export Web Page...</b> from the menu "
"bar.\n"
msgstr ""

#: tips.cc:79
msgid ""
"<p>...that you can purge completed todo's in one step? Go to the\n"
"<b>File</b> menu and choose <b>Purge Completed</b>.\n"
msgstr ""

